From ea89c53c1de09241eb22b26eeb5ebd0390fbfe58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ronghua Zeng <ronghuaz@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 00:02:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: enterprise: add WPA3-ENT PEAP/MSCHAPv2, fix optional
 creds and TTLS

Add WIFI_SECURITY_TYPE_EAP_WPA3_ENT_PEAP_MSCHAPV2 security type for
WPA3-Enterprise (802.1X + PMF) with PEAP/MSCHAPv2 as the EAP method.
Register it in the EAP config table and validation path.

Introduce supplicant_config_enterprise_network(), a new entry point for
drivers that manage 802.11 auth/assoc directly (e.g. fullmac). It calls
wpas_add_and_config_network() with do_connect=false so wpa_supplicant is
pre-configured before qapi_WLAN_Commit() fires, avoiding a race where
EVENT_ASSOC arrives before the EAP network is registered. The do_connect
parameter is threaded through all existing call sites (STA and AP) with
do_connect=true to preserve prior behavior.

Fix optional enterprise credential handling: client cert/key, phase-2
cert/key, anonymous_identity, and key_passwd are now each guarded by a
length check before being pushed to wpa_supplicant. This prevents
(e.g. PEAP/MSCHAPv2 needs no client certificate).

Fix EAP-TTLS phase-2 method string: "auth=MSCHAPV2" is only valid when
the inner method is MSCHAPV2 tunneled inside PEAP; for TTLS the correct
wpa_supplicant keyword is "autheap=MSCHAPV2".

Fix default eap_ver initialisation to 0 in __wifi_args_to_params(); the
previous value of 1 caused PEAP to negotiate PEAPv1 by default, which
some RADIUS servers reject.

Move wifi_enterprise_cert_sec_tags enum from wifi_certs.c into the
public wifi_certs.h header so that out-of-tree cert loader modules can
use the same tag values without duplication. Add public declarations for
wifi_load_certs_from_fs(), wifi_list_certs(), and wifi_clear_certs().

Extend wifi_certs.c process_certificates() to treat -ENOENT as
"credential not registered" rather than a hard error, allowing
phase-2 certs to be absent for methods that do not require them.

Add wifi load_certs shell subcommand (CONFIG_WIFI_SHELL_RUNTIME_CERTIFICATES
+ CONFIG_FILE_SYSTEM_LITTLEFS) with getopt_long parsing:
-c/--ca, -k/--key, -e/--cert, -p/--key-pass, -l/--list, --clear.
This replaces the former ad-hoc /lfs path syntax.

Fix EVENT_EAPOL_RX memory leak in supp_main.c: the src and data buffers
allocated by the event producer were never freed in the socket handler
cleanup path.

Add ETH_P_EAPOL to the supported protocol list in sockets_packet.c so
that EAPOL frames can be received on a raw packet socket.

Conditionalise optional hostap crypto sources in CMakeLists.txt:
aes-eax (EAP-IKEv2 only), fips_prf_internal and milenage (EAP-SIM/AKA
only) are now compiled only when the corresponding EAP method Kconfig is
enabled, reducing flash usage for typical enterprise deployments.

Remove the unconditional "select NET_CONNECTION_MANAGER" from
MCUMGR_TRANSPORT_UDP Kconfig; this dependency was pulling in connection
manager even for configurations that do not use it.

Change-Id: I1f5d7ea0ee375aaf9eeee50f960d5eafee3d4e89
